findings.suggestion:
Apply the same null-guard pattern used in `getSubGroupsCount()` to all three `getSubGroupsStream` overloads. For each overload, store `modelSupplier.get()` in a local, return `Stream.empty()` if the model is null, otherwise delegate. For example:

```java
@Override
public Stream<GroupModel> getSubGroupsStream(String search, Boolean exact, Integer firstResult, Integer maxResults) {
    if (isUpdated()) return updated.getSubGroupsStream(search, exact, firstResult, maxResults);
    GroupModel model = modelSupplier.get();
    return model == null ? Stream.empty() : model.getSubGroupsStream(search, exact, firstResult, maxResults);
}
```

Return `Stream.empty()` rather than `null` because the `GroupModel.getSubGroupsStream()` contract states "Never returns {@code null}". Apply the identical pattern to the `(String, Integer, Integer)` and `(Integer, Integer)` overloads. Consider extracting a helper `private GroupModel getDelegateOrNull()` to avoid repeating the null-check at every call site. Additionally, add a regression test that exercises the `GET /groups/{id}/children` endpoint concurrently with group deletion to cover this path.

