findings.suggestion:
Retain the thread reference and join it before asserting:

```java
Thread reader = new Thread(() -> { ... });
reader.start();
// delete groups...
deletedAll.set(true);
reader.join(5000);
assertThat(caughtExceptions, Matchers.empty());
```

Better: use a `CountDownLatch` per iteration so the main thread can wait for the reader to complete a full request that overlapped with deletions, then flip `deletedAll` and join. This converts the test from a best-effort race detector into a deterministic regression test.

