findings.body:
The PR (commit 4def149a50 "Fix NPE when accessing group concurrently") adds null-model tolerance to the concurrent-delete race in the infinispan GroupAdapter.getSubGroupsCount(): when the underlying group is deleted by another thread, modelSupplier.get() returns null and the method returns null instead of NPEing. The same race condition is reachable in GroupUtils.populateGroupHierarchyFromSubGroups's parent walk, but that walk applies NO null tolerance, so the fix is incomplete.

End A (the relied-on tolerance, model/infinispan/src/main/java/org/keycloak/models/cache/infinispan/GroupAdapter.java:272-276):
    public Long getSubGroupsCount() {
        if (isUpdated()) return updated.getSubGroupsCount();
        GroupModel model = modelSupplier.get();
        return model == null ? null : model.getSubGroupsCount();
    }
This explicitly treats a null model (group concurrently deleted) as a tolerated condition and returns null. The JPA adapter corroborates that getGroupById-style lookups yield null under this race: model/jpa/.../GroupAdapter.java:183-186 filters its stream with `.map(realm::getGroupById).filter(Objects::nonNull)` and the comment "In concurrent tests, the group might be deleted in another thread, therefore, skip those null values."

End B (the changed location that does NOT honor the same tolerance, services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/utils/GroupUtils.java:46-60):
    while(currGroup.getParentId() != null) {
        GroupModel parentModel = session.groups().getGroupById(realm, currGroup.getParentId());   // line 47 — can return null when parent is concurrently deleted
        if (!AdminPermissionsSchema.SCHEMA.isAdminPermissionsEnabled(realm)) {
            if(!groupEvaluator.canView() && !groupEvaluator.canView(parentModel)) {               // line 51 — dereferences parentModel (null) via canView
                groupIdToGroups.remove(currGroup.getId());
                break;
            }                }
        GroupRepresentation parent = groupIdToGroups.computeIfAbsent(currGroup.getParentId(),
            id -> toRepresentation(groupEvaluator, parentModel, full));                            // line 57 — toRepresentation(parentModel=null, full) NPEs
        if (subGroupsCount) {
            populateSubGroupCount(parentModel, parent);                                           // line 60 — parentModel.getSubGroupsCount() NPEs
        }
        ...
    }

Disagreement: End A treats `model == null` as a tolerated condition produced by the concurrent-delete race. End B performs a fresh `session.groups().getGroupById(realm, parentId)` lookup that the JPA adapter confirms can return null under that same race, then dereferences the result at lines 51, 57, and 60 without any null check. `toRepresentation(groupEvaluator, parentModel, full)` calls `ModelToRepresentation.toRepresentation(GroupModel group, boolean full)` (server-spi-private/.../ModelToRepresentation.java:150-152), whose first statement is `rep.setId(group.getId())` — an immediate NPE when `group` is null. `populateSubGroupCount(parentModel, parent)` calls `parentModel.getSubGroupsCount()` (GroupUtils.java:90) — also an immediate NPE.

Concrete consequence: for any group whose parent chain is walked by populateGroupHierarchyFromSubGroups (called from GroupsResource.java:113 and GroupResource.java), if a parent group is deleted by another thread between the subGroup lookup and the `session.groups().getGroupById` parent lookup at line 47, the admin groups endpoint throws an NPE — the exact class of concurrent-access NPE the PR targets. The fix is incomplete: the same null-model tolerance applied to getSubGroupsCount must also be applied to the parent walk.

