findings.suggestion:
Three changes are needed together to make this test actually verify concurrent safety:
1. Store the reader thread reference and call `thread.join()` (with a timeout) before the assertion at line 157, e.g.:
   ```java
   Thread reader = new Thread(() -> { ... });
   reader.start();
   // ... deletions ...
   deletedAll.set(true);
   reader.join(5000);
   assertThat(caughtExceptions, Matchers.empty());
   ```
2. Replace `Integer.MAX_VALUE` with a bounded value (e.g., `groupUuuids.size() + 10`) and add `Thread.sleep(10)` inside the reader loop to avoid a tight spin-loop that saturates a CPU core.
3. Fix the null-return contract violation in `GroupAdapter.getSubGroupsCount()`: `return model == null ? 0L : model.getSubGroupsCount();` instead of `return model == null ? null : model.getSubGroupsCount();` — this ensures the test would actually catch a regression if a future caller auto-unboxes the result.
